BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Guild Speaker Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260912T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260912T143000
UID:260824E2bgK5NzikONRfmxp4WwWg
DESCRIPTION:Rick Kelley \n\nBrown County Art History/Q&A\n\nSaturday\, Sep
 tember 12\n\n1pm – 2:30pm \n\nBrown County Inn  \n\nAs part of the 2026
  Art Colony Weekend and in conjunction with the Art Colony Auction Preview
 \, join us for a fascinating journey into the history of one of America’
 s most celebrated art colonies. \n\nBrown County historian and resident Ri
 ck Kelley will share his deep knowledge of the Brown County Art Colony and
  the remarkable artists who came to these hills seeking inspiration\, comm
 unity\, and a place to call home. Through engaging stories\, personal insi
 ghts\, and historical anecdotes\, Rick brings the past to life\, revealing
  the people\, places\, and events that shaped Brown County’s rich artist
 ic legacy. Rick will invite audience members to ask questions and share in
  the conversation. \n\nThis event is free and open to the public.
LOCATION:Brown County Art Guild
URL:https://browncountyartguild.org/event/guild-speaker-series/
X-SOURCE:Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
